    "result_text": "The full test suite passes \u2014 **44 tests, 0 failures, 0 errors, BUILD SUCCESS**.\n\n## Summary\n\nI updated the locality derivation in `OwnerMapper.java` so it prefers the postcode over the city.\n\nThe `locality(Owner)` method now:\n1. **Looks up the region by postcode range first** \u2014 NSW `2000-2099`, VIC `3000-3099`, QLD `4000-4099` (via a new `regionFromPostcode` helper that safely handles null/non-4-digit values).\n2. **Falls back to the city-to-region table** (`Sydney\u2192NSW`, `Melbourne\u2192VIC`, `Brisbane\u2192QLD`, else `UNKNOWN`) only when the postcode is absent or in no known range (via a new `regionFromCity` helper).\n\nBoth helpers are `private` (matching the existing `normalizeHouseholdField` pattern) so MapStruct doesn't treat them as implicit String\u2192String conversions.\n\nThis returns the same region for known cities (e.g. Sydney \u2192 NSW) but disambiguates same-named cities, since a VIC-range postcode on an otherwise-unknown city now yields VIC \u2014 exactly what the new `Cp30Tests` asserts, while the existing `Cp17Tests` (postcode absent \u2192 city fallback) still passes.",
