    "probe_text": "Confirmed against the source. Here is the complete ordered sequence for **POST /api/owners** (`OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner`, lines 450\u2013476).\n\n## Phase 0 \u2014 Framework Bean Validation (before the method body)\n\nThe endpoint interface is `@Validated` and the body is `@Valid @RequestBody OwnerFieldsDto`, so Spring enforces the DTO constraints first; failures \u2192 **400** (`MethodArgumentNotValidException`):\n\n- `firstName` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..30)`, `@Pattern` (letters + up to two `' -`-joined parts)\n- `lastName` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..30)`, `@Pattern` (same, trailing `.` allowed)\n- `address` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..255)`\n- `city` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..80)`\n- `postcode` \u2014 `@Pattern(\"^[0-9]{4}$\")` (nullable)\n- `telephone` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..20)`, `@Pattern(\"^[-0-9 ()+.]*$\")`\n- `email` \u2014 `@Size(max 255)`, `@Email` (nullable)\n- `registrationDate` \u2014 `@Valid` (nullable)\n\nAlso a class/method-level authorization side-effect: `@PreAuthorize(\"hasRole(OWNER_ADMIN)\")` (denied \u2192 **403**).\n\n## Phase 1 \u2014 Controller body, in exact order\n\n1. **Normalize address** (`setAddress(normalizeAddress(...))`) \u2014 trim, collapse whitespace, uppercase, expand ST\u2192STREET / RD\u2192ROAD / AVE\u2192AVENUE. *(mutates the DTO)*\n2. **`validateRequiredFields`** \u2014 firstName/lastName/address/city/telephone must be non-blank, else `RequiredFieldsMissingException` (**400**). *(second blank-check on top of Bean Validation, run against the normalized address)*\n3. **`validatePostcode(postcode, city)`** \u2014 if postcode present: 4 digits **and** within the city's regional range (NSW 2000\u20132099, VIC 3000\u20133099, QLD 4000\u20134099), else `InvalidFieldsException` (**400**).\n4. **Normalize telephone** (`normalizeTelephone`) \u2014 strip spaces/dashes/brackets, apply `+61` default and drop leading `0`, validate E.164 (`+` then 8\u201315 digits) plus per-country national-length check (61\u21929, 1\u219210), else `InvalidFieldsException` (**400**).\n5. **`requireCityHasCapacity(city)`** \u2014 loads all owners; reject if the city already has \u2265 50 owners \u2192 `CityAtCapacityException` (**409**).\n6. **Normalize email** (`normalizeEmail`) \u2014 null/blank \u2192 null; otherwise must match email pattern, returned lowercased, else `InvalidFieldsException` (**400**).\n7. **Map DTO \u2192 `Owner`** (`ownerMapper.toOwner`) \u2014 id & pets ignored.\n8. **Overwrite** `owner.telephone` and `owner.email` with the normalized values.\n9. **`requireUniqueIdentity(owner)`** \u2014 loads all owners; collision based **solely on matching normalized telephone** \u2192 `DuplicateOwnerIdentityException` (**409**). *(Note: `sharesHousehold`/household-duplicate rules are not consulted anywhere.)*\n10. **Compute registration date** \u2014 `effectiveDate = owner.registrationDate ?? LocalDate.now()`, then `toBusinessDay(...)` (Sat\u2192+2 days, Sun\u2192+1 day); `owner.setRegistrationDate(...)`. *(mutates the owner)*\n11. **`requireDailyLimitNotReached(registrationDate)`** \u2014 loads all owners; if \u2265 100 already share that registration date \u2192 `DailyOwnerLimitException` (**429**).\n12. **Set bulk-signup warning** \u2014 `owner.setBulkSignupWarning(isBulkSignup(registrationDate))`, true if > 80 owners already share that date. *(side-effect on the owner)*\n13. **`clinicService.saveOwner(owner)`** \u2014 persistence, see Phase 2.\n14. **Audit log** \u2014 `AUDIT.info(\"owner created id=... customerCode=... registrationDate=... membershipLevel=...\")` to the dedicated `\"AUDIT\"` logger (membershipLevel computed via the mapper). *(side-effect)*\n15. **Map `Owner` \u2192 `OwnerDto`** (`toOwnerDto`) \u2014 derives displayName, initials, householdId (SHA-256), identityKey, membershipNumber, membershipLevel, locality, contactPreference for the response.\n16. **Set `Location: /api/owners/{id}` header** and return **201 CREATED**.\n\n## Phase 2 \u2014 Service `saveOwner` (@Transactional), only when the owner is new and the field is still null\n\n17. **`customerCode`** \u2190 `generateCustomerCode` = `<CITY3>-<LAST3>-<NNNN>`, where NNNN = (existing owners in that city) + 1.\n18. **`namesakeCount`** \u2190 count of existing owners with same first+last name (case-insensitive).\n19. **`householdMemberCount`** \u2190 count of existing owners sharing normalized lastName+address, +1.\n20. **`ownerRepository.save(owner)`** \u2192 `em.persist` (jpa profile) or Spring Data save.\n\n## Phase 3 \u2014 Persistence-time validation\n\n21. On flush, Hibernate re-validates the **entity** constraints: `firstName`/`lastName` `@NotEmpty` (via `Person`), `address`/`city` `@NotEmpty`, and `telephone` `@NotEmpty @Pattern(\"^\\+[0-9]{8,15}$\")` \u2014 so the normalized E.164 phone must satisfy that stricter pattern at persist time.\n\n**Notes:** There are **no** JPA lifecycle callbacks, `@EntityListeners`, or JPA auditing anywhere \u2014 `registrationDate` is set manually in the controller (step 10), not by `@CreatedDate`. The `sharesHousehold` DTO flag is parsed but never read. Handlers exist for `DuplicateOwnerTelephoneException` / `DuplicateOwnerEmailException` / `DuplicateOwnerHouseholdException`, but nothing in the create path throws them \u2014 duplicate detection is consolidated into the telephone-only check at step 9."
